{
  "id": "note-from-the-author",
  "kind": "introduction",
  "sourceKind": "author-note",
  "label": "Note from the Author",
  "title": "NOTE FROM THE AUTHOR",
  "shortTitle": "NOTE FROM THE AUTHOR",
  "sourceRange": [
    49,
    69
  ],
  "headerSourceParagraphs": {
    "title": 49
  },
  "elements": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "The Human Fiction is not written to convince, correct, or conclude."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 50
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "It is written to observe."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 51
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "What it observes is not the world as an external reality…"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 52
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "but the way reality is continuously constructed through thought, memory, and interpretation."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 53
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Most of what feels like “understanding” is not final truth…"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 54
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "it is ongoing narration."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 55
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "A process that turns raw experience into structured meaning."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 56
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "This work does not oppose meaning."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 57
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "It only points to how meaning is formed in the first place."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 58
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Nothing in these pages requires belief."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 59
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "And nothing requires rejection."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 60
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Because both belief and rejection arise from the same mechanism — interpretation."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 61
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "The intention here is not to provide answers…"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 62
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "but to make the process of asking visible."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 63
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "And once the process is seen clearly…"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 64
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "its automatic authority begins to soften on its own."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 65
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "The Human Fiction does not end with a conclusion."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 66
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "It ends with a shift in seeing —"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 67
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "that experience does not need to be explained to be real."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 68
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "It only needs to be seen."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 69
    }
  ],
  "index": 5,
  "suppressHeaderNumber": true,
  "file": "chapters/05-note-from-the-author.json"
}
